		{
			"controlType": "layout_directive_comment",
			"display": "{B=White,Light Blue} 1{T=.3}{C=Black,White}{B=White,Light Blue} 1{T=.3}{C=Black,White}{B=White,Light Blue}{Data=e9334388_de48_4404_bf51_f9ec9ebd46fe}{I:'$$code.action.commentOut'} {C=#104+150+1120,White}Things of note about this component:  The component implements a 'responsive' design. On a phone, th...",
			"displayODFlat": "{Data=e9334388_de48_4404_bf51_f9ec9ebd46fe}{I:'$$code.action.commentOut'}",
			"idInternal": "e9334388_de48_4404_bf51_f9ec9ebd46fe",
			"displayOD": "{Data=e9334388_de48_4404_bf51_f9ec9ebd46fe}{I:'$$code.action.commentOut'}",
			"displayODtree": "{B=White,Light Blue}{B=White,#104+150+112}{Data=e9334388_de48_4404_bf51_f9ec9ebd46fe}{I:'$$code.action.commentOut'} {C=#104+150+1120,White}Things of note about this component:...",
			"crc": "4294959533",
			"v": {
				"comment": "Things of note about this component:\r\n\r\nThe component implements a 'responsive' design. On a phone, the menu is shown on demand when the user taps on the menu icon in the Panel header.\r\nOn the other hand, on a tablet, where there is more space, the menu is always shown on the right side of the screen.\r\n\r\n1. The list of choices shown in the menu is a defined in the data source for the 'menuList' list control.\r\n2. The 'menuList' uses CSS Icons from the 'Font-Awesome' icon font library which is bundled with Alpha Anywhere\r\n3. Notice that in the List control the 'control-type' for the Icon column has been set to 'CSSIcon'\r\n4. In the List, an onClick event handler has been defined. This event handler closes the slide out menu (if the menu is not always visible)\r\n   and gives focus to the appropariate PanelCard for the menu item selected.\r\n5. 'onSwipe' events are defined for the PanelLayout so that the menu can be shown (if it is not always visible) by swiping to the right, and hidden by swiping to the left.\r\n6. The minimum size on the 'MASTERPANEL' has been set to 500px. This means that on most phones, the MenuPanel will be hidden regardless\r\n   of the orientation of the phone and will be shown when the user taps on the icon in the header. However, on tablets, the MENUPANEL will always be shown. \r\n   If you want the menu to always be hidden, even on a tablet, then simply set the minimum size to a large number.\r\n7. To customize the component for your own use, delete the menu items you don't need from the menu list and put controls in each of the PanelCards (e.g. 'Action1', 'Action2', etc.)\r\n8. The label in the PanelHeader is dynamically set by Javascript code in the List's onClick event. The PanelHeader has a span with an Id and the Javascript in the onClick event \r\n   updates the inner HTML of this span with the name of the menu item that was selected.\r\n\r\n",
				"info": {
					"level": 0,
					"isContainerStart": false,
					"isTabControlStart": false,
					"isContainerEnd": false,
					"isTabControlEnd": false,
					"isTabPaneEnd": false,
